{
  "comment": "Agent NDA grading (agentnda.net 0.1.0-draft, 3, 5, 7.1, 11). An NDA asks the recipient to do things in private, so its promises are 'recorded', the facts around them (parties, instants, signatures, acts) are 'evidence', and NOTHING in an agreement is 'enforced': a clause graded 'enforced' is refused as the false enforcement claim (Agent SoW 3 rule 1). The one enforced step, a board releasing a gated body after a valid acceptance, is defined in Agent RFP 5.11 and does not appear in an agreement. Also pinned: the closed lists and what absence means in each (a category, activity, exclusion or need_to_know value left out is not covered and MUST NOT be inferred; absent subcontractors means none; absent survival is no survival period, never a default), and the derivation of the lifecycle state from signatures, acts and instants. Each case edits the base document: an edit maps a dotted path to its new value, and the value \"<removed>\" deletes the member. THE FIXTURE IS THE AUTHORITY: when a test against it fails, fix the implementation; when the fixture itself is believed wrong, change it only with a spec change alongside.",
  "version": 1,
  "spec": "Agent NDA 0.1.0-draft: 3 (gradient), 5 (clauses, with 5.1 multilateral agreements and 5.5 flow-down), 6.2 (mandates), 7.1 (states), 8.1 (whether a party is bound), 11 (conformance)",
  "grades": {
    "comment": "11: the grade each clause MUST carry. Any other grade does not validate; 'enforced' on any clause is reported as the false enforcement claim.",
    "fixed": {
      "parties": "evidence",
      "purpose": "recorded",
      "covers": "recorded",
      "disclosure": "recorded",
      "survival": "recorded",
      "exclusions": "recorded",
      "compelled": "recorded",
      "at_end": "recorded",
      "termination": "evidence"
    },
    "false_enforcement_message": "an Agent NDA clause cannot be enforced: no runtime can refuse a recipient's private use of what it holds (Agent NDA 3)",
    "render_rule": "A renderer shows every clause's grade and never presents a promise as enforced, even for a body released by an enforced board step."
  },
